# DRY + SOLID (practical)

## DRY

- Copy-paste twice → extract (helper in `src/lib/`, shared component, Zod schema, or site config).
- Reuse `src/data/site.ts`, `src/data/propuestas.json`, tRPC routers, and existing components before adding new ones.
- Validation once at the door (Zod / env) — don't re-validate the same rule in three places with different logic.

## SOLID (light)

- **S** — one file / component / router = one job.
- **O** — extend via config/data (proposals JSON, site tokens) instead of hardcoding new cases into UI.
- **D** — UI talks to tRPC; tRPC talks to DB. Don't import `postgres` from components.

## When not to DRY

Don't force a shared abstraction across two things that only look similar. Duplication is cheaper than a wrong abstraction.
